# The flagship pattern from kexhq/kex#171's own design: a template file's
# text, brought in with Kex.embed (M2) and lowered by Template.text (M3),
# in one expression — `Template.text(Kex.embed("..."))`. Kex.embed folds to
# a literal before Template.text's own argument-shape check ever runs (see
# expand()'s step 0), so this composes with no special handling either side
# needs to know about the other.

main do
  let greet = Template.text(Kex.embed("lib/compiled/embed_template.ket"))
  IO.printLine(greet("world"))
end
